  "summary": "Viral images circulating on social media appear to show Sai Pallavi and Vijay Sethupathi filming on Kolkata's Howrah Bridge for a Mani Ratnam project. The original article content is currently inaccessible due to an Access Denied error, but photos and reports continue to spread online.",
  "content": "Viral images and short clips circulating on social media appear to show actors Sai Pallavi and Vijay Sethupathi on the Howrah Bridge in Kolkata, reportedly shooting for director Mani Ratnam's latest project. The images have drawn attention because of the pedigree of the cast and the iconic location, prompting fans to share and comment widely across platforms.\n\nThe reported shoot on the Howrah Bridge, one of Kolkata's best-known landmarks, prompted onlookers and photographers to post pictures and reactions online. While production companies sometimes stage shoots at prominent public locations, details about the film, scene being shot or official statements from the cast and crew have not been confirmed in the public domain at the time of reporting.\n\nAttempts to access the original source article returned an error page instead of full copy. The returned content included an \"Access Denied\" response and an edge network reference, as follows:\n\nAccess Denied\nReference #18.87014017.1785199935.5786995a https://errors.edgesuite.net/18.87014017.1785199935.5786995a\n\nThe error suggests the page or resource could not be retrieved for this report. As a result, available information relies on the viral social posts and secondary sharing; official confirmations from the film's production team or the actors remain pending.\n\nFans and observers are watching for an official announcement or clearer images from verified sources. Until then, the viral photos continue to fuel speculation about the scale and location of the shoot and about Mani Ratnam's next film choices.",
